{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/RandomGraphs\/documentation\/RandomGraphs"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isDigraphical"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"inDegrees"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"outDegrees"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"D. R. Fulkerson. Zero-one matrices with zero trace. "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pacific Journal of Mathematics","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 10(3),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"831–836 (1960); Wai-Kai Chen. On the realization of a (p, s)-digraph with prescribed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degrees. "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Journal of the Franklin Institute","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 281(5), 406–422 (1966); Richard P. Anstee."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Properties of a class of (0, 1)-matrix covering problems. "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Discrete Mathematics","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 41(1),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1–9 (1982),"}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"with the vertices ordered by out-degree, non-increasing; the order among equal out-degrees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not change the answer (Annabell Berger, “A note on the characterization of digraphic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequences”, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discrete Mathematics"}]},{"type":"text","text":" 314, 38–41, 2014). With a = the out-degrees and b = the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in-degrees in that order, it checks Σ a = Σ b and, for each k,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Σᵢ≤ₖ aᵢ ≤ Σᵢ≤ₖ min(bᵢ, k − 1) + Σᵢ>ₖ min(bᵢ, k)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A negative degree or one of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" or more makes the pair not digraphical."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n): a counting sort, then one pass.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inDegrees.count == outDegrees.count"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/randomgraphs\/isdigraphical(indegrees:outdegrees:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Function","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/RandomGraphs\/DegreeSequences.swift#L90","fileName":"DegreeSequences.swift"},"symbolKind":"func","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDigraphical","